    "reading": {
        "body": "The top 55 AI repositories accumulated 2.7 million stars total, growing by roughly 2,400 stars per day over the past two weeks, indicating sustained developer attention to foundational tools and frameworks rather than consolidation around any single project.\n\nTensorFlow leads by stars, followed by AutoGPT and Ollama, but the distribution is flat enough that infrastructure projects (PyTorch, LangChain, llama.cpp) compete directly with application-layer tools (AutoGPT, browser-use, OpenHands) for developer mindshare. Nearly all 55 repositories received commits within the past two days, suggesting the ecosystem is not stratified into active and abandoned projects but rather operates as a dense layer of continuous development.\n\nThe data reflects GitHub activity only and measures engagement through a social metric, stars, rather than actual compute consumption or deployment. It shows where developers are writing and iterating on code, which matters for AI because training frameworks and inference engines must maintain active communities to stay viable as the field shifts. But it does not reveal which repositories consume the most compute resources, which are actually deployed at scale, or whether star growth corresponds to genuine capability advances or primarily to adoption of simpler, more accessible tools.",
